#. 6.2->settings-schema.json->app-rules->tooltip
#. 6.7.6->settings-schema.json->app-rules->tooltip
msgid ""
"A list of applications with special effect rules. The application can be a "
"desktop file name or a WM_CLASS name. Click a rule, then click a cell to "
"change it. Hover over an effect and click the gear icon beside it to "
"configure custom effect settings for that application."
msgstr ""

#. 6.2->settings-schema.json->app-rules-button->description
#. 6.7.6->settings-schema.json->app-rules-button->description
msgid "Pick a window to add…"
msgstr ""

#. 6.2->settings-schema.json->app-rules-button->tooltip
#. 6.7.6->settings-schema.json->app-rules-button->tooltip
msgid ""
"Click this, then click any window to add an entry for its application to the "
"list above. Press Esc or right-click to cancel."
msgstr ""

#. 6.2->settings-schema.json->random-include->tooltip
#. 6.7.6->settings-schema.json->random-include->tooltip
msgid ""
"Defines which effects are included in the randomized sets for each window "
"event type. When 'Randomized' is selected for any event on the General tab "
"these sets are used. Hover over a ticked box and click the gear icon beside "
"it to configure custom effect settings, used when that effect is randomly "
"chosen for that event."
msgstr ""

